Are you an experienced forklift operator who feels right at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to work for a stable company where you’ll work alongside a small, close-knit team to ensure everything runs smoothly? Then we have a great opportunity for you!

For a client in Weert, we’re looking for an experienced forklift operator who enjoys working the night shift. You’ll be joining a large logistics company where safety, teamwork, and a pleasant work environment are top priorities.

What will you be doing?

As a forklift operator, you’ll be responsible for moving goods efficiently and safely within the warehouse. You’ll spend most of your workday operating the forklift. Together with four colleagues, you’ll ensure that all pallets and goods are placed in the correct locations and that outbound orders are ready on time.

Your duties will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking orders and preparing them for shipment;
- Scanning goods;
- Moving pallets and goods within the warehouse;
- Preparing outgoing orders for transport.

You’ll be operating a forklift with double forks, loading from the side. Do you have experience with this? If so, be sure to read on!

You’ve already gained considerable experience operating a forklift and understand how important it is to work safely and accurately. You’re flexible, keep a cool head during busy periods, and are comfortable working two different shifts.

In addition:

- You have recent experience as a forklift operator;
- You hold a valid forklift operator’s certificate;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You are available full-time;
- You work with precision and always put safety first.

Are you strong in planning, organizing, and maintaining oversight in a dynamic logistics environment? Do you enjoy improving processes while supporting a fast-growing operation? Then the role of Operations Planner in Moerdijk could be your next career move. Working in one of the largest and most modern warehouses in the Benelux, you will play a crucial role in ensuring the smooth flow of daily order operations. You will make sure everything behind the scenes is perfectly coordinated, allowing the operation to perform at its best.

As an Operations Planner, you will be responsible for the warehouse's outbound planning activities. You will ensure that customer orders are properly prepared, scheduled, and processed within the operation. Working closely with the operational teams, you will act as a key link between systems, planning, and execution.

Your responsibilities include:

- Processing daily customer requests and forecasts;
- Planning and prioritizing outbound orders within the system;
- Aligning capacity and operational activities with the warehouse floor;
- Coordinating pick-and-pack processes to ensure orders are processed efficiently;
- Acting as the first point of contact for operational planning-related questions;
- Monitoring the progress, timing, and accuracy of order flows;
- Ensuring that all process steps are followed strictly from start to finish;
- Supporting the optimization of planning and logistics processes.

For this position, we are looking for someone who excels at planning and can maintain a clear overview in a complex logistics environment.

- Relevant experience within logistics (planning and/or warehouse operations);
- Strong organizational and administrative skills;
- Ability to work under pressure and effectively prioritize tasks;
- Good command of the English language (required);
- Comfortable working with computers and digital systems;
- Available to work full-time in a two-shift schedule.

Can your colleagues in production count on spotless and hygienic workspaces? Do you enjoy staying active on the job? Then you can quickly start working as a cleaner or industrial cleaner at Luiten! Your full-time workday starts around 9:00 or 10:00 AM. You’ll change into your work attire, grab your cleaning materials and equipment, and begin moving between the various production areas with your high-pressure cleaner.
Not only will you thoroughly clean the production spaces, but you’ll also ensure that the machines used to process and package meat—and all related materials—are meticulously cleaned. You take care of your own work, following HACCP and hygiene regulations carefully. In addition to cleaning, you make sure that every area is safe to enter and ready for use.
No need for an activity tracker here, as you’ll definitely get plenty of daily movement in this role! Together with your friendly, multicultural team, you’ll ensure production can start on time and in a clean environment.

- You are available full-time from Monday till Friday;
- Overtime doesn’t wear you out—instead, it makes your wallet fuller;
- You speak Dutch or English, essential for safety on the work floor;
- Some experience with cleaning and/or sanitation is a plus.

